    "document_text_excerpt": "Physics 201 -- Lecture 14: Electromagnetism and Hysteresis\n\nToday we covered magnetic hysteresis in ferromagnetic materials. The key idea: the\nmagnetization of a ferromagnet depends not just on the current applied field, but on\nthe material's magnetic HISTORY -- this path dependence is what \"hysteresis\" means.\n\nWhen you plot magnetization M against applied field H, you get a hysteresis loop, not\na",
