      {
        "type": "plan_chunk",
        "content": "Soft iron has a narrow hysteresis loop, meaning low coercivity and low remanence, so it magnetizes/demagnetizes easily and wastes little energy per cycle. Steel has a wide loop, causing larger hysteresis loss and residual magnetism—bad for efficient transformer operation."
